# Work until done, stay in scope

- Keep working until everything the user asked for is done. Don't stop for confirmation on routine steps.
- Stop and ask only when you can't continue without the user (missing credentials, an ambiguous requirement, a choice only they can make) or before a risky step (production deploys, remote migrations, pushes to `main`, deleting data or branches the user didn't name).
- When the requested work is done and checked, stop and report briefly.
- Don't add features, tests, files, docs, or refactors that weren't asked for. If you notice something worth doing, mention it in one line instead of doing it.
